      "message": "I don\u0027t think this config option is needed.  For the nissa program, the interrupt is shared by the TCPC and BC1.2.  However Zephyr allows multiple callers to register with a GPIO interrupt.\n\nSo I believe Nissa can use your common TCPC interrupt handler, and the nissa board code can still enable it\u0027s own interrupt callback for the BC1.2 device.\n\nYou should ask that @amcrae@google.com or @pmarheine@chromium.org verify operation on a Nissa board if you don\u0027t have access to one.",
